    "https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/fds_ind_ap_id_08_2026/": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Industrial Design",
      "description": "Assistant Professor in Industrial Design – Career@UM Skip to content Search for: Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 Assistant Professor in Industrial Design Apply for this job now Assistant Professor in Industrial Design Industrial Design (Reference No.: FDS/IND/AP/ID/08/2026) Academic Staff The Department of Industrial Design of the Faculty of Design invites applications for the position of Assistant Professor in Industrial Design. The Faculty of Design offers postgraduate degree programmes in Industrial Design, and will offer undergraduate degrees programme in Industrial Design according to the current plan. Based in Macao, the Department of Industrial Design is committed to “integrated design-driven innovation”, supporting the appropriate economic diversification of Macao and cultivating top-tier design talent for the Greater Bay Area and beyond, including the global stage. Leveraging the industrial resources of the Greater Bay Area, the Department focuses on intelligent design methodologies and industrial processes, highly integrated smart product design, and comprehensive research and practice in sustainability. The curriculum emphasizes the integration of “design + technology + business,” covering areas such as user research, product development, digital manufacturing, ergonomics, human-computer interaction, and service design. Through studios, field research, and international exchange projects, students acquire solid professional skills and critical thinking abilities. We seek internationally minded faculty members with strong design portfolios, graduate teaching ability, and a commitment to mentoring students and contributing to the development of the Faculty of Design. Qualifications 1. A doctoral degree (or equivalent terminal degree) in Industrial Design or a closely related field; 2. Demonstrated potential for excellence in teaching, research and application-based innovation, with expertise in one or more of the following areas: a. sustainable product-service-system design and circular innovation, including lifecycle thinking, sustainable materials, systems thinking and service-led strategies for ecological and social transformation; b. digital-physical design integration and intelligent product design, including smart and connected products, tangible interaction, physical computing, digital fabrication and responsive materials; c. advanced industrial design and product development, including product architecture, design for manufacturing, materials and CMF, advanced prototyping and human factors; d. advanced and emerging design methodologies, including research-through-design, practice-led and practice-based research, critical and speculative design, and responsible or more-than-human approaches; 3. A strong record or demonstrable potential in practice-led and application-oriented design, supported by real-world projects, impactful implementations or industry-academic collaborations; 4. Proficiency in mainstream industrial design software, prototyping tools and processes, including physical computing, additive and digital manufacturing, and experimentation with conventional, smart and sustainable materials; 5. Evidence of strong research and creative potential through peer-reviewed academic publications and, where applicable, recognized creative outputs such as design patents, curated exhibitions, funded projects or international design awards; 6. Experience teaching and mentoring in studio-based, transdisciplinary or research-intensive design courses, with the ability to contribute to postgraduate teaching and supervision; 7. Fluency in English is required. Proficiency in Chinese is considered an asset, particularly for cross-cultural communication, community- and industry-engaged research, and collaboration in Macao and the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area. The selected candidate is expected to assume duty subject to the mutual agreement of the both parties. Remuneration A taxable annual remuneration starting from MOP855,400 (approximately USD105,600) will be commensurate with the successful applicants’ academic qualification and relevant professional experience. The current local maximum income tax rate is 12% but is effectively around 5% – 7% after various discretionary exemptions. Apart from competitive remuneration, UM offers a wide range of benefits, such as medical insurance, provident fund, on-campus accommodation/housing allowance and other subsidies. Further details on our package are available at: https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/learn-more/ . Application Procedure Applicants should visit https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ for more details, and apply ONLINE. Applicant should submit a cover letter that addresses the academic qualifications and a detailed Curriculum Vitae with the contact information of three references (phone numbers and email addresses), research statement, teaching philosophy and a portfolio (for design practice categories). Additionally, applicants should provide no more than six samples of academic writing/publications/essays/catalogues, and sample syllabi of classes previously taught. Publication samples could be emailed to fds.enquiry@um.edu.mo if less than 20MB. Shortlisted candidates may be requested to submit additional materials. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Applicants may consider their applications not successful if they are not invited for an interview within 3 months of application. Human Resources Section, Office of Administration University of Macau, Av. da Universidade, Taipa, Macau, China Website: https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ ;  Email: vacancy@um.edu.mo Tel: +853 8822 8699;  Fax: +853 8822 2412 The effective position and salary index are subject to the Personnel Statute of the University of Macau in force. The University of Macau reserves the right not to appoint a candidate. Applicants with less qualification and experience can be offered lower positions under special circumstances. ***Personal data provided by applicants will be kept confidential and used for recruitment purpose only*** **Under the equal condition of qualifications and experience, priority will be given to Macao permanent residents** Word document Word document (zip) PDF (view with Acrobat Reader) Download the application form only when applying through this online system is not likely. When not applying through this website, besides completing the application form, please submit your CV, copy of academic certificates (diplomas), ID or passport copy and declaration of employment (for civil servant only) to the above postal address, e-mail address or fax no. Click here to download the Acrobat Reader ensonho Ho Io San 2026-09-03T23:42:19+08:00 This site is best viewed in Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, Safari or Microsoft Edge. Copyright © Office of Administration (ADMO). All rights reserved.    | UM Home | UM News | UM Event Calendar Page load link Go to Top"
    },
    "https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/iapme_faap_08_2026/": {
      "title": "Full/Associate/Assistant Professor in Materials Science and Engineering",
      "description": "Full/Associate/Assistant Professor in Materials Science and Engineering – Career@UM Skip to content Search for: Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 Full/Associate/Assistant Professor in Materials Science and Engineering Apply for this job now Full/Associate/Assistant Professor in Materials Science and Engineering Materials Science and Engineering (Reference No.: IAPME/FAAP/08/2026) Academic Staff The Institute of Applied Physics and Materials Engineering (IAPME) is inviting applications for academic positions at the rank of Full/Associate Professor/Assistant Professor. For more information about the institute, please refer to the website: http://iapme.um.edu.mo/ IAPME is committed to the balanced integration of fundamental and technology application research, which serves as an innovative bridge between fundamental science and engineering. The interdisciplinary nature of IAPME enables realization of the different research strengths of the university in the scientific engineering solutions as well as in the coping of future technological challenges. At the current stage, the key research areas include environmental materials, photo-electric and electro-optic conversion materials, catalytic and energy materials, materials design and simulation, soft smart materials for wearable and biomedical applications, AI+ science, etc.. The Institute aims to cultivate outstanding, forward-looking, and innovative disciplinary directions that push the boundaries of fundamental science while enabling transformative industrial applications. Qualifications Applicants must hold a PhD degree in a related field. Preference will be given to candidates with postdoctoral experience. Candidates should demonstrate strong potential or established excellence in research and teaching, with a proven record of high-quality publications in reputable international journals and relevant academic experience. The rank of appointment will be determined based on the candidate’s qualifications, achievements, and demonstrated impact in their field. The selected candidate is expected to assume duty in Spring 2027. Remuneration A taxable annual remuneration starting MOP1,250,200 (approximately USD154,350) for the position of Full Professor, MOP1,052,800 (approximately USD129,980) for the position of Associate Professor and MOP855,400 (approximately USD105,600) for the position of Assistant Professor will be commensurate with the successful applicants’ academic qualification and relevant professional experience. The current local maximum income tax rate is 12% but is effectively around 5% – 7% after various discretionary exemptions. Apart from competitive remuneration, UM offers a wide range of benefits, such as medical insurance, provident fund, on-campus accommodation/housing allowance and other subsidies. Further details on our package are available at: https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/learn-more/ . Application Procedure Applicants should visit https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ for more details, and apply ONLINE . Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Applicants may consider their applications not successful if they are not invited for an interview within 3 months of application. Human Resources Section, Office of Administration University of Macau, Av. da Universidade, Taipa, Macau, China Website: https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ ;  Email: vacancy@um.edu.mo Tel: +853 8822 8690;  Fax: +853 8822 2412 The effective position and salary index are subject to the Personnel Statute of the University of Macau in force. The University of Macau reserves the right not to appoint a candidate. Applicants with less qualification and experience can be offered lower positions under special circumstances. ***Personal data provided by applicants will be kept confidential and used for recruitment purpose only*** ** Under the equal condition of qualifications and experience, priority will be given to Macao permanent residents** Word document Word document (zip) PDF (view with Acrobat Reader) Download the application form only when applying through this online system is not likely. When not applying through this website, besides completing the application form, please submit your CV, copy of academic certificates (diplomas), ID or passport copy and declaration of employment (for civil servant only) to the above postal address, e-mail address or fax no. Click here to download the Acrobat Reader kasperso So Ka Chon 2026-09-02T23:42:08+08:00 This site is best viewed in Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, Safari or Microsoft Edge. Copyright © Office of Administration (ADMO). All rights reserved.    | UM Home | UM News | UM Event Calendar Page load link Go to Top"
