    "https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/fah_saa_aa_08_2026/": {
      "title": "Senior Administrative Assistant/Administrative Assistant for the Faculty of Arts and Humanities",
      "description": "Senior Administrative Assistant/Administrative Assistant for the Faculty of Arts and Humanities – Career@UM Skip to content Search for: Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 Senior Administrative Assistant/Administrative Assistant for the Faculty of Arts and Humanities Apply for this job now Senior Administrative Assistant/Administrative Assistant for the Faculty of Arts and Humanities -- (Reference No.: FAH/SAA/AA/08/2026) Administrative Staff The Faculty of Arts and Humanities (FAH) of the University of Macau invites applications for the position of Senior Administrative Assistant/Administrative Assistant at a taxable monthly salary ranging from MOP25,380 to MOP43,240 (index 270 – 460). Responsibilities Provide administrative support and handle clerical work in the General Office of the Faculty, such as writing proposals, letters, etc.; Assist in budgeting and monitoring of budgetary resources; Provide technical support and analysis for superior’s decision making; Assist in information collection and compilation as requested by sub-units; Handle enquiries and provide communication channels between faculty members and students; Perform other duties and ad-hoc tasks as assigned. Requirements Bachelor’s degree or above in accounting, finance, or a business-related discipline; possession of Master’s degree will be an advantage; Minimum 3 years of full-time work experience, 2 years of which must be working in accounting/auditing related field, or in higher education institution; Candidates from secondary school with English as medium of instruction is highly preferable; High proficiency in written Chinese and English, spoken Mandarin, English and Cantonese; knowledge of Portuguese is an advantage; Attention to details and strong logical thinking skills; Strong interpersonal and communication skills, and able to work both independently and in a team; Self-motivated, with a strong sense of responsibility and competent in multitasking and prioritizing tasks. Application Procedure Applicants should visit https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ for more details and apply ONLINE on or before 10 September 2026 . Application screening will be based on requirements listed above. Please indicate the education qualification obtained and describe relevant work experience clearly in the Curriculum Vitae and application form. The contact points are: Human Resources Section, Office of Administration University of Macau, Av. da Universidade, Taipa, Macau, China Website: https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/;  Email: vacancy@um.edu.mo Tel: +853 8822 8699;  Fax: +853 8822 2412 The effective position and salary index are subject to the Personnel Statute of the University of Macau in force. The University of Macau reserves the right not to appoint a candidate. Applicants with less qualification and experience can be offered lower positions under special circumstances. ***Personal data provided by applicants will be kept confidential and used for recruitment purpose only*** **Under the equal condition of qualifications and experience, priority will be given to Macao permanent residents** Word document Download the application form only when applying through this online system is not likely. When not applying through this website, besides completing the application form, please submit your CV, copy of academic certificates (diplomas), copy of academic transcripts, ID or passport copy and declaration of employment (for civil servant only) to the above postal address, e-mail address or fax no. ensonho Ho Io San 2026-09-03T23:42:10+08:00 This site is best viewed in Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, Safari or Microsoft Edge. Copyright © Office of Administration (ADMO). All rights reserved.    | UM Home | UM News | UM Event Calendar Page load link Go to Top"
    },
    "https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/fah_elc_sii_08_2026/": {
      "title": "Senior Instructor/Instructor of English",
      "description": "Senior Instructor/Instructor of English – Career@UM Skip to content Search for: Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 Senior Instructor/Instructor of English Apply for this job now Senior Instructor/Instructor of English English (Reference No.: FAH/ELC/SII/08/2026) Academic Staff The English Language Centre (ELC) is committed to empowering students to succeed in University studies and in life by engaging them in English, academic, and global skills learning. The ELC seeks to achieve its goals through the provision of courses in English for academic purposes, a writing centre, co-curricular language learning activities and organizing summer programmes for pre-sessional students. The ELC of the Faculty of Arts and Humanities invites applications for the position of Senior Instructor/Instructor of English. Qualifications Applicants must possess a Master’s degree in TESOL/TEFL/ELT/English Education (or related fields). Applicants should have extensive EAP/ESP teaching experience at the tertiary level or equivalent, preferably teaching EFL/ESL students in English-medium higher education context. Eligible candidates should demonstrate experience in (1) curriculum and material development in teaching English for academic purposes (four skills, grammar and vocabulary, academic skills and strategies), and (2) technology-enhanced classroom learning as well as developing e-learning exercises. Updated knowledge and experience in current pedagogy, assessment, programme planning and activity organisation will be an advantage. The successful candidates should possess the following abilities: effective ELT pedagogy in student-centred approaches, strong ability to build rapport with and motivate students, organizational skills, communication skills, collegiality, teamwork and leadership skills. Excellent command of English is expected. The ability to speak Chinese is not required. The candidate is expected to engage in the Centre’s committee works and projects, and provide professional services to the University and the community. Academic research and publication are not required for the positions, but a specific pedagogy-oriented research interest/agenda is welcome. The appointed instructor(s) is expected to rotate and teach in the summer programme during the student summer recess period. The selected candidate is expected to assume duty in August 2027 Remuneration A taxable annual remuneration starting from MOP559,300 (approximately USD69,050) will be commensurate with the successful applicant’s academic qualification and relevant professional experience. The current local maximum income tax rate is 12% but is effectively around 5% – 7% after various discretionary exemptions. Apart from competitive remuneration, UM offers a wide range of benefits, such as medical insurance, provident fund, oncampus accommodation/housing allowance and other subsidies. Further details on our package are available at: https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/learn-more/ . Application Procedure Applicants should visit https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ for more details, and apply ONLINE. The application should include 1) a cover letter, 2) a curriculum vitae with names and contacts of 3 referees, one of whom should be from a current or recent employment (only referees of shortlisted candidates will be contacted); 3) a teaching portfolio that includes (a) a statement of teaching philosophy, (b) a record of institutional-administered teaching evaluations/student feedbacks, and (c) sample lesson plans and teaching materials created by the applicant; and 4) academic certificates and transcripts. Review of applications will continue until the position(s) is/are filled. Applicants may consider their applications not successful if they are not invited for interview within 3 months of application. Human Resources Section, Office of Administration University of Macau, Av. da Universidade, Taipa, Macau, China Website: https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ ;  Email: vacancy@um.edu.mo Tel: +853 8822 8699;  Fax: +853 8822 2412 The effective position and salary index are subject to the Personnel Statute of the University of Macau in force. The University of Macau reserves the right not to appoint a candidate. Applicants with less qualification and experience can be offered lower positions under special circumstances. ***Personal data provided by applicants will be kept confidential and used for recruitment purpose only*** **Under the equal condition of qualifications and experience, priority will be given to Macao permanent residents** Word document Word document (zip) PDF (view with Acrobat Reader) Download the application form only when applying through this online system is not likely. When not applying through this website, besides completing the application form, please submit your CV, copy of academic certificates (diplomas), ID or passport copy and declaration of employment (for civil servant only) to the above postal address, e-mail address or fax no. Click here to download the Acrobat Reader ensonho Ho Io San 2026-09-03T23:42:15+08:00 This site is best viewed in Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, Safari or Microsoft Edge. Copyright © Office of Administration (ADMO). All rights reserved.    | UM Home | UM News | UM Event Calendar Page load link Go to Top"
    },
    "https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/iaibs_ai_faap_08_2026/": {
      "title": "Full/Associate/Assistant Professor in Artificial Intelligence",
      "description": "Full/Associate/Assistant Professor in Artificial Intelligence – Career@UM Skip to content Search for: Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 Full/Associate/Assistant Professor in Artificial Intelligence Apply for this job now Full/Associate/Assistant Professor in Artificial Intelligence Artificial Intelligence (Reference No.: IAIBS/AI/FAAP/08/2026) Academic Staff The Institute of Artificial Intelligence and Brain Sciences (IAIBS) invites applications for the position of Full/Associa te/Assistant Professor in Artificial Intelligence. It will be a joint position with the Department of Artificial Intelligence (AIX) of the Faculty of Information Science and Computing (FIC). This position intends to complement and strengthen existing staff expertise. We are seeking candidate with a proven track record in scientific research, an innovative research vision, and a commitment to education. IAIBS aims to become an internationally leading interdisciplinary research institute by advancing deep integration and innovation of artificial intelligence and brain sciences. It aspires to establish itself as a key hub for AI and brain science in the Greater Bay Area and globally. It is expected that high-profile research work will be carried out through these platforms to produce a number of key scientific outputs and discoveries with world influence. Qualifications PhD degree in Computer Science, AI or related areas; Preference will be given to candidates with specializations in Brain-Inspired Artificial Intelligence, Emotional AI, Neuromorphic Computing, and Trustworthy AI; Strong background in Computer Science, AI or related disciplines, and extensive research and teaching experience at the tertiary education level; Good team player for participating in various aspects of the activities of the centre, institute, and university and serving the profession. The selected candidate is expected to assume duty in 2027. Remuneration A taxable annual remuneration starting from MOP1,250,200 (approximately USD154,350) for the position of Full Professor, MOP1,052,800 (approximately USD129,980) for the position of Associate Professor and MOP855,400 (approximately USD105,600) for the position of Assistant Professor will be commensurate with the successful applicants’ academic qualification and relevant professional experience. The current local maximum income tax rate is 12% but is effectively around 5% – 7% after various discretionary exemptions. Apart from competitive remuneration, UM offers a wide range of benefits, such as medical insurance, provident fund, on-campus accommodation/housing allowance and other subsidies. Further details on our package are available at: https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/learn-more/ . Application Procedure Applicants should visit https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ for more details, and apply ONLINE . Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Applicants may consider their applications not successful if they are not invited for an interview within 3 months of application. Human Resources Section, Office of Administration University of Macau, Av. da Universidade, Taipa, Macau, China Website: https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ ;  Email: vacancy@um.edu.mo Tel: +853 8822 8578;  Fax: +853 8822 2412 The effective position and salary index are subject to the Personnel Statute of the University of Macau in force. The University of Macau reserves the right not to appoint a candidate. Applicants with less qualification and experience can be offered lower positions under special circumstances. ***Personal data provided by applicants will be kept confidential and used for recruitment purpose only*** ** Under the equal condition of qualifications and experience, priority will be given to Macao permanent residents** Word document Word document (zip) PDF (view with Acrobat Reader) Download the application form only when applying through this online system is not likely. When not applying through this website, besides completing the application form, please submit your CV, copy of academic certificates (diplomas), ID or passport copy and declaration of employment (for civil servant only) to the above postal address, e-mail address or fax no. Click here to download the Acrobat Reader dorachau Chau I Cheng 2026-09-02T23:42:09+08:00 This site is best viewed in Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, Safari or Microsoft Edge. Copyright © Office of Administration (ADMO). All rights reserved.    | UM Home | UM News | UM Event Calendar Page load link Go to Top"
    },
    "https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/fba_mmi_mktg_aap_08_2026/": {
      "title": "Associate/Assistant Professor in Marketing",
      "description": "Associate/Assistant Professor in Marketing – Career@UM Skip to content Search for: Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 Associate/Assistant Professor in Marketing Apply for this job now Associate/Assistant Professor in Marketing Marketing (Reference No.: FBA/MMI/MKTG/AAP/08/2026) Academic Staff The Department of Management and Marketing at the Faculty of Business Administration (FBA) invites applications for the position of Associate/Assistant Professor in Marketing . FBA is one of the largest faculties in the University and a well-established full-service business faculty with AACSB, AMBA and EQUIS accreditations. It is a distinctive flagship business school in the region with key responsibilities in business and management education and nurturing the leadership talents for the development of Macao and beyond as its mission states. It bridges academic education with real-world practice and proactively engages with industry and professional bodies, thus has made a significant impact on industry and society. FBA provides education in both traditional and emerging subjects of business and management, ranging from Accounting, Finance, Business Economics, Information Systems and Management, Marketing, General Management, to specialised Integrated Resort and Tourism Management. Our programmes are delivered at all levels of higher education including Undergraduate, Postgraduate, PhD, MBA, EMBA, DBA and Executive Education. Moreover, we strongly encourage cross-disciplinary teaching, learning and research both within the University and internationally to enhance innovation and career development for our students and academics alike. Our programmes are highly recognised by the industry which leads to excellent employability of our students. More details about the Faculty are available at: https://fba.um.edu.mo/ . The Department of Management and Marketing at FBA is looking for top-quality scholars to join the department as Associate/Assistant Professor in Marketing with specialization in Quantitative Marketing. Faculty members in Marketing have published in top marketing journals (e.g., Journal of Consumer Research , Journal of Marketing Research , Journal of Marketing , and Journal of Consumer Psychology ) and other premier business and psychology outlets (e.g., Journal of International Business Studies , Organization Science , Journal of Personality and Social Psychology , and Journal of Applied Psychology ). The Department provides its faculty members with excellent research support including a start-up research grant, a reasonable teaching load, and access to sophisticated facilities. The Department has an active research seminar series and an established doctoral program that is fast-growing. In line with this strategic development, the Department of Management and Marketing aims to build a strong team of Marketing scholars in the coming years. Hence, FBA is conducting a global recruitment of Associate/Assistant Professor in Marketing. Qualifications Applicants should (1) have obtained a PhD degree (or close to completion) in Marketing, Strategy, International Business, Innovation or closely related fields; (2) demonstrate evidence of ability or potential to conduct impactful research and publish in top-tier journals in Marketing and related fields; and (3) have the commitment to teaching excellence, at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels. Applicants for Associate Professor position should have a well-established track record of research excellence substantiated by publication in high-quality journals, effective academic leadership in significant research endeavors, and a strong commitment to mentoring junior researchers. Successful applicants are also expected to make appropriate contributions to university and community services. The selected candidate is expected to assume duty in August 2027, or at any time subject to the mutual agreement of the both parties. Remuneration The remuneration will be competitive and commensurate with the successful applicants’ academic qualification and relevant professional experience. The current local maximum income tax rate is 12% but is effectively around 5% – 7% after various discretionary exemptions. Apart from competitive remuneration, UM offers a wide range of benefits, such as on-campus accommodation or housing allowance, medical insurance, provident fund, and other subsidies. Further details on our package are available at: https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/learn-more/ . Application Procedure Applicants should visit https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ for more details, and apply ONLINE . Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Applicants should provide contact information of at least three referees, including telephone number and email address. For Assistant Professor position, referees will be invited to send reference letters directly to the University before the review process begins. For Associate Professor position, referees will be invited to submit reference letters in due course. Applicants may consider their applications not successful if they are not invited for an interview within 3 months of application. Human Resources Section, Office of Administration University of Macau, Av. da Universidade, Taipa, Macau, China Website: https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ ; Email: vacancy@um.edu.mo Tel: +853 8822 8406; Fax: +853 8822 2412 The effective position and salary index are subject to the Personnel Statute of the University of Macau in force. The University of Macau reserves the right not to appoint a candidate. Applicants with less qualification and experience can be offered lower positions under special circumstances. ***Personal data provided by applicants will be kept confidential and used for recruitment purpose only*** ** Under the equal condition of qualifications and experience, priority will be given to Macao permanent residents** Word document Word document (zip) PDF (view with Acrobat Reader) Download the application form only when applying through this online system is not likely. When not applying through this website, besides completing the application form, please submit your CV, copy of academic certificates (diplomas), ID or passport copy and declaration of employment (for civil servant only) to the above postal address, e-mail address or fax no. Click here to download the Acrobat Reader michelleieong Ieong Lam Ian 2026-09-03T23:42:33+08:00 This site is best viewed in Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, Safari or Microsoft Edge. Copyright © Office of Administration (ADMO). All rights reserved.    | UM Home | UM News | UM Event Calendar Page load link Go to Top"
    },
    "https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/fba_fbe_fin_aap_08_2026/": {
      "title": "Associate/Assistant Professor in Finance",
      "description": "Associate/Assistant Professor in Finance – Career@UM Skip to content Search for: Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 Associate/Assistant Professor in Finance Apply for this job now Associate/Assistant Professor in Finance Finance (Reference No.: FBA/FBE/FIN/AAP/08/2026) Academic Staff The Department of Finance and Business Economics (DFBE) at Faculty of Business Administration (FBA) invites applications for the position of Associate/Assistant Professor in Finance . FBA is one of the largest faculties in the University and a well-established full-service business faculty with AACSB, AMBA, and EQUIS accreditations. It is a distinctive flagship business school in the region, playing a vital role in business and management education with key responsibilities in nurturing the leadership talents for the development of Macao and beyond as its mission states. It bridges academic education with real-world practice and actively engages with industry and professional bodies, strives to be a world-class business faculty, aiming to create a significant impact on the business community and society, thus contributing to the economic and sustainable development of Macao and beyond. FBA provides education in both traditional and emerging subjects of business and management, ranging from Accounting, Finance, Business Economics, Information Systems and Management, Marketing, General Management, to specialised Integrated Resort and Tourism Management. Our programmes are delivered at all levels of higher education including Undergraduate, Postgraduate, PhD, MBA, EMBA, DBA and Executive Education. Moreover, we strongly encourage cross-disciplinary teaching, learning and research both within the University and internationally to enhance innovation and career development for our students and academics alike. Our programmes are highly recognised by industry which leads to excellent employability of our students. For example, our professional accredited accounting programmes have obtained full course exemptions by ACCA, CIMA, CPA Australia, HKICPA which makes them top accounting programmes in Mainland China, Macao and Hong Kong recognized by professional accounting bodies. More details about the Faculty are available at: https://fba.um.edu.mo/ . DFBE is a fast-growing group in finance and business economics. The faculty members in DFBE have publication records in top finance, management, and economics journals (e.g., Journal of Finance, Journal of Financial Economics, Review of Financial Studies, Management Science, Journal of Econometrics, Journal of Business & Economic Statistics, Journal of Monetary Economics, Journal of Development Economics , etc.). The Department provides its faculty members with excellent research support including a start-up research grant, reasonable teaching load, and state-of-the-art facilities. The Department aims to build a stronger team of finance scholars in the research fields of asset pricing, corporate finance, fintech, and financial economics. Hence, we are conducting a global recruitment of Associate/Assistant Professor in Finance. Qualifications Applicants should (1) be a promising or established scholar with a doctoral degree (or close to completion) in Finance, Management, Economics, or a closely related field; (2) have ability to teach undergraduate, postgraduate and PhD courses; and (3) have ability to publish research papers in high-ranked journals in related fields. The selected candidate is expected to assume duty by August 2027, or at any time subject to the mutual agreement of the both parties. Remuneration Remuneration offered will be competitive and commensurate with the successful applicants’ academic qualification and relevant professional experience. The current local maximum income tax rate is 12% but is effectively around 5% – 7% after various discretionary exemptions. Apart from competitive remuneration, UM offers a wide range of benefits, such as medical insurance, provident fund, on-campus accommodation/housing allowance and other subsidies. Further details on our package are available at: https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/learn-more/ . Application Procedure Applicants should visit https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ for more details, and apply ONLINE. Review of applications will continue until the positions are filled. Applicants should provide contact information of at least three referees, including telephone number and email address. For Assistant Professor position, referees will be invited to send reference letters directly to the University before the review process begins. For Associate Professor position, referees will be invited to submit reference letters in due course. Applicants may consider their applications not successful if they are not invited for an interview within 3 months of application. Human Resources Section, Office of Administration University of Macau, Av. da Universidade, Taipa, Macau, China Website: https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ ;  Email: vacancy@um.edu.mo Tel: +853 8822 8406; Fax: +853 8822 2412 The effective position and salary index are subject to the Personnel Statute of the University of Macau in force. The University of Macau reserves the right not to appoint a candidate. Applicants with less qualification and experience can be offered lower positions under special circumstances. ***Personal data provided by applicants will be kept confidential and used for recruitment purpose only*** ** Under the equal condition of qualifications and experience, priority will be given to Macao permanent residents** Word document Word document (zip) PDF (view with Acrobat Reader) Download the application form only when applying through this online system is not likely. When not applying through this website, besides completing the application form, please submit your CV, copy of academic certificates (diplomas), ID or passport copy and declaration of employment (for civil servant only) to the above postal address, e-mail address or fax no. Click here to download the Acrobat Reader michelleieong Ieong Lam Ian 2026-09-03T23:42:34+08:00 This site is best viewed in Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, Safari or Microsoft Edge. Copyright © Office of Administration (ADMO). All rights reserved.    | UM Home | UM News | UM Event Calendar Page load link Go to Top"
    },
    "https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/fba_fbe_mec_aap_08_2026/": {
      "title": "Associate/Assistant Professor in Microeconometrics",
      "description": "Associate/Assistant Professor in Microeconometrics – Career@UM Skip to content Search for: Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 Associate/Assistant Professor in Microeconometrics Apply for this job now Associate/Assistant Professor in Microeconometrics Economics specializing in Microeconometrics (Reference No.: FBA/FBE/MEC/AAP/08/2026) Academic Staff The Department of Finance and Business Economics at the Faculty of Business Administration (FBA) invites applications for the position of Associate/Assistant Professor in Economics specializing in Microeconometrics, with a particular focus on causal inference . FBA is one of the largest faculties in the University and a well-established full-service business faculty with AACSB, AMBA and EQUIS accreditations. It is a distinctive flagship business school in the region with key responsibilities in business and management education and nurturing the leadership talents for the development of Macao and beyond as its mission states. It bridges academic education with real-world practice and proactively engages with industry and professional bodies, thus has made a significant impact on industry and society. FBA provides education in both traditional and emerging subjects of business and management, ranging from Accounting, Finance, Business Economics, Information Systems and Management, Marketing, General Management, to specialised Integrated Resort and Tourism Management. Our programmes are delivered at all levels of higher education including Undergraduate, Postgraduate, PhD, MBA, EMBA, DBA and Executive Education. Moreover, we strongly encourage cross-disciplinary teaching, learning and research both within the University and internationally to enhance innovation and career development for our students and academics alike. Our programmes are highly recognised by the industry which leads to excellent employability of our students. More details about the Faculty are available at: https://fba.um.edu.mo/ . The Department of Finance and Business Economics at FBA is looking for top-quality scholars to join the department as Associate/Assistant Professor in Economics with a specialization in Microeconometrics. Faculty members of our department have an impressive record of publications in premier economics and finance journals, which include but are not limited to the Journal of International Economics , Journal of Econometrics , International Economic Review , Journal of Development Economics , Econometric Theory , Journal of Finance , Journal of Financial Economics , and Review of Financial Studies . In addition, several faculty members hold editorial roles in esteemed academic journals. As a department, we are committed to providing exceptional research support to our faculty, inclusive of a start-up research grant, a reasonable teaching load, and access to sophisticated facilities. We also champion a dynamic research seminar series and oversee an expanding doctoral program. Guided by our strategic development plan, we aim to consolidate a robust team of business economics scholars in the upcoming years. As such, FBA is currently embarking on a worldwide recruitment drive for the position of Associate/Assistant Professor in Economics with a specialization in Microeconometrics. Qualifications Applicants should (1) be a promising or established scholar with a doctoral degree in Economics, or a closely related field; (2) have the ability to teach undergraduate, postgraduate, and PhD courses; and (3) have ability to publish research papers in highly ranked journals in related fields. Applicants for Associate Professor position should have a well-established track record of research excellence substantiated by publication in highly ranked journals, and a strong commitment to mentoring junior researchers. The selected candidate is expected to assume duty in August 2027, or at any time subject to the mutual agreement of the both parties. Remuneration The remuneration will be competitive and commensurate with the successful applicants’ academic qualification and relevant professional experience. The current local maximum income tax rate is 12% but is effectively around 5% – 7% after various discretionary exemptions. Apart from competitive remuneration, UM offers a wide range of benefits, such as on-campus accommodation or housing allowance, medical insurance, provident fund, and other subsidies. Further details on our package are available at: https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/learn-more/ . Application Procedure Applicants should visit https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ for more details, and apply ONLINE . Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Applicants should provide contact information of at least three referees, including telephone number and email address. For Assistant Professor position, referees will be invited to send reference letters directly to the University before the review process begins. For Associate Professor position, referees will be invited to submit reference letters in due course. Applicants may consider their applications not successful if they are not invited for an interview within 3 months of application. Human Resources Section, Office of Administration University of Macau, Av. da Universidade, Taipa, Macau, China Website: https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ ;  Email: vacancy@um.edu.mo Tel: +853 8822 8406; Fax: +853 8822 2412 The effective position and salary index are subject to the Personnel Statute of the University of Macau in force. The University of Macau reserves the right not to appoint a candidate. Applicants with less qualification and experience can be offered lower positions under special circumstances. ***Personal data provided by applicants will be kept confidential and used for recruitment purpose only*** ** Under the equal condition of qualifications and experience, priority will be given to Macao permanent residents** Word document Word document (zip) PDF (view with Acrobat Reader) Download the application form only when applying through this online system is not likely. When not applying through this website, besides completing the application form, please submit your CV, copy of academic certificates (diplomas), ID or passport copy and declaration of employment (for civil servant only) to the above postal address, e-mail address or fax no. Click here to download the Acrobat Reader michelleieong Ieong Lam Ian 2026-09-03T23:42:34+08:00 This site is best viewed in Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, Safari or Microsoft Edge. Copyright © Office of Administration (ADMO). All rights reserved.    | UM Home | UM News | UM Event Calendar Page load link Go to Top"
    },
    "https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/fsc_rp_08_2026/": {
      "title": "Research Positions in the Faculty of Science",
      "description": "Research Positions in the Faculty of Science – Career@UM Skip to content Search for: Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 Home Login Career Page Career Opportunities Learn More Contact Us ENG 中文 Research Positions in the Faculty of Science Apply for this job now Research Positions in the Faculty of Science Science (Reference No.: FSC/RP/08/2026) Research Staff The Faculty of Science (FSC) invites applications for the position of research personnel in the following areas: Biological Sciences, Chemistry, Mathematics, Physics and related disciplines. Initial appointment is up to 12 months with a possibility of renewal upon mutual agreement and funding availability. As part of a strategic expansion, UM recently established five science and technology faculties through the restructuring of part of its existing faculties. In which, FSC aspires to become a world-class hub for fundamental scientific research and education. It actively promotes interdisciplinary collaboration in key applied areas, including applied mathematics, applied physics and materials engineering, and smart city technologies. These initiatives aim to bridge fundamental research and real-world applications, enhancing the societal impact of scientific advancement. Qualifications Visiting Fellows: A doctoral degree and professional rank at Associate Professor or above in related disciplines; a solid research record and expertise. Postdoctoral Fellows: A doctoral degree in related disciplines; a solid record of publication and scientific training. Research Assistants: A bachelor’ s degree or above in related disciplines; with relevant research and/or project experience The selected candidate is expected to assume duty as soon as possible. Remuneration Remuneration and appointment rank offered will be commensurate with the successful applicants’ academic qualification and relevant professional experience. The current local maximum income tax rate is 12% but is effectively around 5% – 7% after various discretionary exemptions. Application Procedure Applicants should visit https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ for more details and apply ONLINE . Review of applications will continue until the positions are filled. Applicants may consider their applications not successful if they are not invited for an interview within 3 months of application. Human Resources Section, Office of Administration University of Macau, Av. da Universidade, Taipa, Macau, China Website: https://career.admo.um.edu.mo/ ; Email: vacancy@um.edu.mo Tel: +853 8822 8690; Fax: +853 8822 2412 The University of Macau reserves the right not to appoint a candidate. ***Personal data provided by applicants will be kept confidential and used for recruitment purpose only*** ** Under the equal condition of qualifications and experience, priority will be given to Macao permanent residents** Word document Word document (zip) PDF (view with Acrobat Reader) Download the application form only when applying through this online system is not likely. When not applying through this website, besides completing the application form, please submit your CV, copy of academic certificates (diplomas), ID or passport copy and declaration of employment (for civil servant only) to the above postal address, e-mail address or fax no. Click here to download the Acrobat Reader kasperso So Ka Chon 2026-09-03T23:42:25+08:00 This site is best viewed in Google Chrome, Mozilla Firefox, Safari or Microsoft Edge. Copyright © Office of Administration (ADMO). All rights reserved.    | UM Home | UM News | UM Event Calendar Page load link Go to Top"
